          "input": [
            "text",
            "image"
          ],
          "$comment": "2026-08-19: k3 collapsed into pure-'!' thinking streams twice in one morning (OpenRouter upstream-node failure). repetition_penalty (heuristic value) makes the single-token attractor less likely; the degenerate-stream-guard extension is the hard containment. Not all upstreams honor repetition_penalty - remove if reasoning feels flattened. Routing prefers the official Moonshot AI deployment, falls back to the pool. NOTE: $comment is only safe at THIS level - samplingParams and openRouterRouting are forwarded verbatim to the API, a $comment inside them 400s the request.",
          "samplingParams": {
            "repetition_penalty": 1.05
          },
          "compat": {
            "openRouterRouting": {
              "order": [
                "Moonshot AI"
              ],
              "allow_fallbacks": true
            }
          }
        },
        "openrouter/auto": {
          "$comment": "OpenRouter prices its router pseudo-models at -1 ('variable, depends on routed model'). Pi multiplies it straight through, so every auto turn subtracts its token count from session cost (footer showed $-150685 on 2026-08-11). Zero it: unknown is honest, negative is wrong. Same -1 sentinel on auto-beta and fusion.",
